---
/**
 * /programmes/ — from the 15 October 2026 landing-page package
 * (docs/2026-10-15_living-craft-landing-pages/programmes/index.html).
 * Staging only: branch feat/programme-pathways must not merge.
 *
 * The markup and the words are the package's, unchanged, except:
 *   * every fee, hour count and the instructor line read from
 *     src/data/programme-offers.ts and facts.ts (PRICING REVIEW: the fees are
 *     not yet calibrated; see that file's header);
 *   * the instructor line reads "Walmart Labs", as the package has it
 *     (approved by the user on 15 October; facts.ts still says "Walmart");
 *   * the enquiry form is RouteForm (the pipeline), not the package's
 *     email draft. See PackageEnquiry.astro for what that dropped.
 * The look is the package's own stylesheet, scoped: see
 * src/styles/templates/programme-package.css.
 *
 * WHAT THIS REPLACED. On `main` this page compares three ROUTES into one offer
 * (open cohort, employer-funded place, enterprise programme). The package
 * replaces that with two PATHWAYS of three offers each. The cohort page at `/`
 * and /programmes/enterprise/ are unchanged, and the October campaign links
 * all point at `/`, so nothing moves or redirects it.
 *
 * OPEN DECISION, FOR SUNIL. The package never mentions the six-week,
 * eight-seat cohort at `/`. Its Design to Deployment has the same 30 live
 * hours and the same ₹1,20,000, but no weeks, no seat cap and no start date.
 * Either it IS the cohort, and `/` and facts.ts must say what these pages say,
 * or it is a second offer, and this hub needs a line pointing at `/`.
 */
import PackagePage from '../../components/programmes/PackagePage.astro';
import PackageEnquiry from '../../components/programmes/PackageEnquiry.astro';
import { practitioner } from '../../data/facts';
import { EXPERIENCE, READINESS_REVIEW_HOURS, hourWord, hoursList, interestsFor, lowestFee } from '../../data/programme-offers';

const title = 'Programmes with Sunil Mathew | The Living Craft';
const description = `Explore agentic-systems programmes and career preparation with ${practitioner.name}. Compare two pathways and choose the support that matches your next step.`;
---

<PackagePage title={title} description={description} path="/programmes/" breadcrumb={['Programmes']} enquire="tell-us-what-you-want-to-achieve">
<section class="hero common-hero">
<div class="hero-copy">
<h1>Build agentic systems.<br>
<span>Prepare for your next career move.</span>
</h1>
<p>Practical programmes with Sunil Mathew for experienced engineers, architects and engineering leaders. Choose hands-on agentic-system development or focused career and interview preparation.</p>
<p>
<a href="#choose-your-pathway">Explore the two pathways</a>
</p>
</div>
<figure class="art common-art">
<img src="/programmes/pathways.webp" alt="A woven gold thread branches towards a system model and a rising personal pathway" width="1513" height="1040" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
</figure>
</section>
<section class="section choices" id="choose-your-pathway">
<h2>Choose your pathway</h2>
<div class="pathway-choices">
<article class="path-choice path-0">
<span class="path-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
<h3>Build Agentic Systems</h3>
<p>You want to understand how an agentic system works, build one and make sound decisions about its behaviour.</p>
<p>Work on a focused agent, a proof of concept or a project taken through deployment. Build, evaluate and revise your work with guidance and feedback.</p>
<p>
<strong>Three live cohort programmes · {hoursList('agentic-systems')} live hours · Fees from {lowestFee('agentic-systems')} per participant</strong>
</p>
<p>
<a href="/programmes/agentic-systems/">Compare agentic-systems programmes</a>
</p>
</article>
<article class="path-choice path-1">
<span class="path-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
<h3>Career Transition &amp; Interview Preparation</h3>
<p>You want clarity about your next role, a plan for moving towards agentic-AI work, or practice before an interview.</p>
<p>Choose a focused mock interview, structured preparation with two mocks, or a career-transition roadmap with personal guidance.</p>
<p>
<strong>Three one-to-one packages · {hoursList('career-preparation')} hours · Fees from {lowestFee('career-preparation')}</strong>
</p>
<p>
<a href="/programmes/career-preparation/">Compare career-preparation packages</a>
</p>
</article>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section practitioner" id="work-with-an-experienced-practitioner">
<figure class="portrait ">
<img src="/programmes/sunil-bookshelf.webp" width="480" height="600" alt="Sunil Mathew seated in front of a bookshelf" loading="lazy">
</figure>
<div>
<h2>Work with an experienced practitioner</h2>
<p>Sunil Mathew brings {EXPERIENCE}. His background includes leading engineering teams and hiring, developing and assessing senior technical professionals.</p>
<p>At The Living Craft, that experience informs the work you do: examining a design, explaining trade-offs, practising a decision and learning from feedback.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section outcome-reading" id="start-with-the-outcome-you-need">
<div class="section-head">
<h2>Start with the outcome you need</h2>
</div>
<div class="section-body">
<p>If your priority is to build technical capability through a working project, explore the Build Agentic Systems pathway.</p>
<p>If your priority is a target role, preparation plan or interview performance, explore Career Transition &amp; Interview Preparation.</p>
<p>You can discuss fit before choosing a programme. A company can also enquire about sponsoring an individual or developing a team&#x27;s capability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section joining" id="how-joining-works">
<h2>How joining works</h2>
<ol>
<li>Share your experience and what you want to achieve.</li>
<li>Discuss the programme scope and your starting point.</li>
<li>Review the schedule, availability and payment terms before deciding.</li>
<li>Join the agreed programme and work through practice and feedback.</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section class="section faq" id="common-questions">
<h2>Common questions</h2>
<div>
<details>
<summary>Can I join one programme on its own?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Yes. Choose the programme that matches your goal and starting point. Each offer has its own scope; you do not need to enrol in the full range.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Does career preparation include technical training?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Career packages help you assess your gaps, plan preparation and practise interviews. The Build pathway provides hands-on technical development through a scoped project.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>Can my employer sponsor me?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Discuss the programme you want to join and your employer&#x27;s requirements. Individual sponsorship and a programme for a whole team are scoped separately.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>What if I need help choosing?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="answer">
<p>Share your experience and goal in an enquiry. For deeper career planning, you can also discuss the {hourWord(READINESS_REVIEW_HOURS)} Career Readiness Review through the Career pathway.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</section>
<PackageEnquiry
  id="tell-us-what-you-want-to-achieve"
  heading="Tell us what you want to achieve"
  intro="Share a little about your experience and the next step you have in mind. The team will discuss programme fit, scope and availability with you."
  action="Send my programme enquiry"
  labels={{"name":"Full name","email":"Email address","role":"Current role","phone":"Phone number, optional","question":"Your goal","interest":"Pathway"}}
  order={["name","email","role","question","interest","phone"]}
  omit={["organisation","discovery","discovery_detail"]}
  choices={{ interest: interestsFor('hub') }}
/>
</PackagePage>
